# /test authorization and code ownership are separate lists.
#
# The `/test allowlist:` line authorizes every infrastructure-team member to
# trigger /test: the commenter, the PR author, and (for fork PRs) the fork
# owner must appear there. GitHub Actions cannot read team membership
# (GITHUB_TOKEN is repository-scoped and has no organization Members
# permission), so the team has to be listed explicitly; a team handle cannot
# be expanded by the workflow.
#
# Keep the allowlist in sync with the team membership:
# https://github.com/orgs/konflux-ci/teams/infrastructure
#
# /test allowlist: @celeztyne @eisraeli @enkeefe00 @filariow @gbenhaim @gcpsoares @glevi-rh @hugares @manish-jangra @mcada @meyrevived @mshaposhnik @oswcab @sadlerap @vsokolen-redhat @wbrefvem
#
# Review ownership:
# - The /test gate definition is owned by the whole infrastructure team, so
#   changing it requires a team review.
# - Every other file is owned by the core reviewers below. The rest of the
#   team is authorized for /test but is not auto-requested for review.
#
# CODEOWNERS applies the LAST matching pattern, so the `*` rule must come
# before the workflow-specific rule.
#
# Individual owners need direct write access; team-derived admin is not enough
# for GitHub's CODEOWNERS validation. The team handle is valid because the
# infrastructure team has admin.

